# nr-office-comrs-switch-excel: xlsx (every one-shot xlsx call and every xlsx session) is served by the Rust host.
# Compiled list: native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/route.rs RUST_HOST_FORMATS = &["docx", "xlsx"] (done in this task).
# Depends on nr-office-comrs-excel-read and nr-office-comrs-excel-edit (and the session/actions tasks they sit on) being applied first
# (the xlsx entries of the readers and editors tables of src/drivers.rs): the Rust host answers every xlsx action only with both.
# pptx stays on powershell.exe; `detect` stays with the docx entry. Nothing was compiled (the lead builds the wave).
# No protocol row, no service, no SERVICE_PENDING name, no Cargo.lock change.

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/Cargo.toml (not owned by this task)
Test target, after `[[test]] name = "switch_word_live"`:

    [[test]]
    name = "switch_excel_live"
    path = "tests/switch_excel_live.rs"

The test target needs no dependency that switch_word_live does not already use (regex, zip, tokio, tokio-util, serde_json,
mixdog-fsio, mixdog-rt) and uses the crate's `com::live` (`Sta`, `create_object`), `com::Obj`, `com::Value`.

## 2. Nothing else: the composer already sets `rust_host_program` for the docx switch; an xlsx call starts the same program.
Tests that build the transport with the shipped list and an xlsx call (transport_route.rs) were updated in this task.
